      "problem": "Evaluate $2^{-3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We find the reciprocal of the base $({\\color{blue}{2}}),$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the *opposite* sign $({{\\color{red}{+3}}}),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{-3} & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2})\\times (\\frac{1}{2})\\times (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1\\times 1\\times 1}{2\\times 2\\times 2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
